  "style": [
    "Address the user politely with “siz” in sentences (e.g. “…ekleyebilirsiniz”); buttons and menu items are short commands without a final full stop (e.g. “Not oluştur”, “Ayarları aç”).",
    "Turkish suffixes must follow vowel harmony, which depends on the value of a placeholder. Never attach a suffix directly to a placeholder: rephrase so it stands alone (e.g. “Not: {title}”), or use an apostrophe form that reads acceptably for any value.",
    "Use the dotted and dotless i correctly (İ/i, I/ı), including in capitals.",
    "Use “ ” quotation marks.",
    "Keep placeholders such as {count} or {title} exactly as written, and reorder them freely to fit the target language's word order.",
    "Keep keyboard symbols and key names (⌘ ⌥ ⇧ ⌃ ↵ Esc Tab Enter Space) and shortcut letters unchanged.",
    "Keep the source's ellipsis “…” and the middle dot “·” as they are.",
    "Translate meaning, not words; prefer the wording established apps on this platform use (Finder, Notes, Obsidian, Notion, Linear)."
  ],
